{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789297575,"nonce":"RYhdcR4OC6wiDwcs3WbI6UbFfhk=","title":"bind_foreign_method_fn and bind_foreign_class_fn are configured but never read","message":"VMConfig declares bind_foreign_method_fn and bind_foreign_class_fn and\nthe README/docs describe them as the host's way to bind foreign classes,\nbut nothing in src/runtime consults them: a ClassMir with foreign_methods\neither dlopens its native_library or, with none, prints \"class 'X' has\nforeign methods but no #!native directive\". A host embedding wren_lift\ntherefore cannot bind foreign methods through the documented callbacks.\nEither wire them into the install path (consulted before the dlopen\nroute, keyed by module, class, is_static, signature as declared) or\nremove them from VMConfig. Found while hosting wren_lift under caribou,\nwhich binds natives onto the installed class directly instead.\n\nRelated, separate: `import \"m\" for A as B` binds B to null (verified with\nwlift alone).","files":null}]}